# Vertex inputs corresponding to scene_buffer_layouts.dl. Application shaders
# choose lighting and effects while sharing the same geometry and transforms.
import lib/shader.dl
import lib/vector.dl

the UI scene shader position means: the vertex input named "position" at location 0 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 3, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader normal means: the vertex input named "normal" at location 1 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 3, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader coordinates means: the vertex input named "coordinates" at location 2 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 2, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader vertex color means: the vertex input named "vertex_color" at location 3 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 3, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader color means: the vertex input named "material_color" at location 11 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader emission means: the vertex input named "material_emission" at location 12 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader surface means: the vertex input named "material_surface" at location 13 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader flags means: the vertex input named "material_flags" at location 14 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "uint", 32)))

the UI scene shader model x means: the vertex input named "model_x" at location 4 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader model y means: the vertex input named "model_y" at location 5 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader model z means: the vertex input named "model_z" at location 6 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader model origin means: the vertex input named "model_origin" at location 7 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader normal x means: the vertex input named "normal_x" at location 8 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 3, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader normal y means: the vertex input named "normal_y" at location 9 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 3, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))
the UI scene shader normal z means: the vertex input named "normal_z" at location 10 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 3, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)))

to get [the UI scene shader world position]:
    set point to the UI scene shader position
    set first to the UI scene shader model x
    set second to the UI scene shader model y
    set third to the UI scene shader model z
    set origin to the UI scene shader model origin
    return a new vector with x (((the element at 0 in first) * (the x of point) + (the element at 0 in second) * (the y of point)) + ((the element at 0 in third) * (the z of point) + (the element at 0 in origin))), y (((the element at 1 in first) * (the x of point) + (the element at 1 in second) * (the y of point)) + ((the element at 1 in third) * (the z of point) + (the element at 1 in origin))) and z (((the element at 2 in first) * (the x of point) + (the element at 2 in second) * (the y of point)) + ((the element at 2 in third) * (the z of point) + (the element at 2 in origin)))

to get [the UI scene shader world normal]:
    set normal to the UI scene shader normal
    set first to the UI scene shader normal x
    set second to the UI scene shader normal y
    set third to the UI scene shader normal z
    return ((first * (the x of normal) + second * (the y of normal)) + third * (the z of normal)) normalized

to get [the UI scene shader clip position of] {vector:point} [through] {@intrinsic("matrix", 4, 4, @intrinsic("type", "float", 32)):camera}:
    return @intrinsic("multiply", camera, @intrinsic("construct", @intrinsic("vector", 4), the x of point, the y of point, the z of point, 1.0))
